@startuml
title udo — delete(path): remove node, then re-save its parent

actor TUI
participant Tree
participant fs

TUI -> Tree : delete(path)
Tree -> Tree : node   = get(path)\nparent = get(path[..last])
alt node is Container
  Tree -> fs : remove_dir_all(node.dir)
end
Tree -> Tree : parent.children.remove(last index)
Tree -> Tree : save(parent path)\n(rewrites parent file -> drops child dir / task row)
Tree --> TUI : Ok

note right of Tree
  - Task: no fs remove — drop row + re-save parent.
  - Root (Global): not deletable.
  - Index-path cursor shifts after a remove →
    TUI refreshes `cursor` afterwards.
end note

@enduml
